GRUB theme "arch-mono" — matches the Plymouth theme and tuigreet of the same name.
Black screen, Arch logo outline with grey glow (same size/position as Plymouth draws it),
minimal centred menu (selected = faint blue pill), countdown = thin blue line + "booting in N".

Build:   python3 gen.py out        (fonts via grub-mkfont from JetBrains Mono, logo from
                                    /usr/share/pixmaps/archlinux-logo.svg)
Install: sudo cp -r --no-preserve=ownership out/. /boot/grub/themes/arch-mono/
         GRUB_THEME="/boot/grub/themes/arch-mono/theme.txt" in /etc/default/grub
         sudo grub-mkconfig -o /boot/grub/grub.cfg

GRUB quirks found while building it:
- font names are "<family> <Regular|Bold> <size>" — a Light weight needs its own family name
- grub-mkfont -r wants ranges only (0x2022-0x2022), and the editor frame needs 0x2500-0x257f
- the progress bar is at least ~24px and stretches its centre piece, so the centre piece is a
  24px strip with a 2px line in the middle
Test without rebooting: grub-mkstandalone -O x86_64-efi (memdisk with grub.cfg + theme) booted
in qemu + OVMF with -device bochs-display,xres=1920,yres=1080, screenshots via monitor screendump.
